Z||000009||mrfixit58||05-19-2001||08:06 AM||||If your lens are dull from the sun, the plastic is just oxidized. I bought some great stuff made by 3M. It's their plastic cleaner and plastic polish. Use the cleaner first, then the polish. It costs about $7.50 per bottle but is enough to last forever.<P>SUCCESS STORY FOLLOWS: The lens covers on my GT looked like someone had slid them across the garage floor. They had deep scratches. I wet sanded them smooth gradually decreasing the size of the paper with the final sanding using 1000 grit. I tried to buff them to a shine using clear coat polish but the still looked dull. <P>That's when I decided to try the 3M stuff. I had to use three application of the cleaner before I used the polish but the end results were GREAT. The lens covers look new. The $15 was a cheap investment.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000010||Songman||05-19-2001||12:53 PM||||What about spray on window tint for the inside of the lenses instead of the film?<P>Of course, you need to get rid of the oxidation first or nothing you do it going to look all that good...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||sjp777||05-19-2001||12:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>What about spray on window tint for the inside of the lenses instead of the film?<P>Of course, you need to get rid of the oxidation first or nothing you do it going to look all that good...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Before I did mine with the window tint film I looked everywhere for spray on tint. Every shop I asked about it in laughed in my face and said that stuff hasn't existed since the 70's. If you know where to get it, spill.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||5
